NEARS-2501 AC2 ("Admin/storage/logs/laravel.log, grepped for the X-Request-Id of the
tracking request fired at tap time, confirms the backend received a track request for
the SAME order id") is UNVERIFIABLE against the current backend build: OrderController::
track_order() (Admin/app/Http/Controllers/Api/V1/OrderController.php:48-94) has ZERO
Log::/report() calls on its success path -- nothing writes an order-id-bearing (or any)
line to laravel.log for a successful track request, regardless of X-Request-Id.

Live proof (2026-08-26, backend on 127.0.0.1:8000, primary tree's Admin/storage/logs/laravel.log):

$ TOKEN=<real Bearer token from POST /api/v1/auth/login for customer@nears.com>
$ RID=2ae39cf3-d09a-4118-90ec-bf27bcc4d4c7   # valid UUIDv4, passes SetRequestId's strict check
$ curl -s -D /tmp/hdrs.txt -o /tmp/body.json \
    "http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/customer/order/track?order_id=158" \
    -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" -H "X-Request-Id: $RID"

Response: HTTP/1.1 200 OK, X-Request-Id echoed back correctly as 2ae39cf3-d09a-4118-90ec-bf27bcc4d4c7,
body correctly contains order 158's data ({"id":158,...,"order_status":"confirmed",...}).

$ grep -F "2ae39cf3-d09a-4118-90ec-bf27bcc4d4c7" Admin/storage/logs/laravel.log
(zero matches -- grep rc=1)

The X-Request-Id round-trip mechanism itself works (SetRequestId middleware, NEARS-564).
What's missing is any Log:: call inside track_order()'s success path to correlate against --
so AC2 as literally worded cannot be demonstrated with the current backend code, independent
of this ticket's own (Flutter-side-only) diff. This pre-dates NEARS-2501's change (the fix
never touches Admin/app/Http/Controllers/Api/V1/OrderController.php) but blocks AC2 as written
for THIS ticket, since AC2 IS one of the two reproduction/verification steps this ticket's own
solution doc calls for.

Needs a decision: add a Log::info() (with the allow-listed endpoint+order_id, PII-safe) to
track_order()'s success path, OR amend AC2 to a different, currently-satisfiable correlation
method.
